1.What is CI/CD?
Contineous Integration - CI
CI means developers frequently integrate their code into a shared repository such as GitHub,
after which automated processes validate/build/test it.

Witout CI:
---------
Developer
|
Writes code
|
Manually builds
|
Manually tests
|
Manully copies files

With CI:
--------
Developer
|
git push
|
GitHub
|
Jenkins
|
Build
|
Test

The goal is to catch problems early and make the build process repeatable.

2.What is Continuos Delivery/Deployment?
Continuos Delivery/Deployment - CD
After CI completes successfully, the application needs to reach an environment.

Code
|
Build
|
Test
|
Deploy

Continuos Delivery normally means software is kept in a deployable state, with production release potentially requiring approval
Continuos Deployment goes further: qualifying chnages are automatically released without a manual production approval.

Today Lab:
----------
Github
|
Jenkins
|
S3

Note: Jenkins performance the deployment automatically

 3.What is Jenkins?
Jenkins is an Open-source automation server widely used to implement CI/CD workflows.

Instead of an engineer repeatedly executing deployment commands, Jekins executes predefined pipeline steps
Example:
--------
Without Jenkins:
----------------
git pull
aws s3 sync . s3://bucket-name
aws cloudfront create-invalidation

Engineer must execute these commands every release.

with Jenkins:
-------------
Developer --> git push
                  |
                Jenkins
                  |
    commands execute automatically

4.Why Jenkins?
Feature:            Purpose:
----------------------------
Automation          Removes repetitive manual deployment
Pipeline            Defines CI/CD workflow
Plugins             Integrate with other systems
Git Integration     Retrives application code
Credentials         Handles secrets securely
Distrubuted builds  Work can run an agents
Build history       Tracks pipeline executions
Logs                Helps troubleshooting
Webhooks            Automatically triggers builds
Pipeline as code    Stores pipeline with application code









